# CODEOWNERS for Model Console.
#
# Format: <pattern> <owner> [<owner>...]
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/managing-repository-settings/about-code-owners
#
# This repo is maintained by a single GitHub identity. The placeholder
# below is intentionally a wildcard handle pointing at the project
# owner; forks should overwrite it with their own user / team. GitHub
# silently drops CODEOWNERS entries that reference identities that
# don't exist on the fork, which is the desired failure mode for
# downstream forks.
#
# Default owner for everything in the repo. Specific paths below
# override this; CODEOWNERS uses last-match-wins semantics.
*                       @llm-init-maintainers

# ---- runtime correctness hot spots -------------------------------------
# Any change to the lifecycle state machine, control plane, or data
# plane changes the shape of the operator-visible contract (phases,
# /api/* surface, /v1/* proxy semantics) and needs a maintainer review
# even on otherwise-mechanical refactors.
/internal/lifecycle/    @llm-init-maintainers
/internal/controlplane/ @llm-init-maintainers
/internal/dataplane/    @llm-init-maintainers

# ---- security / supply chain ------------------------------------------
# Anything under .github/workflows changes the CVE / govulncheck /
# release-signing posture.
/.github/workflows/     @llm-init-maintainers

# ---- release artifacts ------------------------------------------------
# CHANGELOG and version-stamped READMEs are part of the release contract;
# reviewing them ensures the docs match the tag.
/CHANGELOG.md           @llm-init-maintainers
